IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tcpss-emergency-calls`

-- Telecommunications (Emergency Call Service) Determination 2019 -- worked cases, from the phone customer's seat. Expected
-- values were written by hand from the deposited Determination (Compilation No. 4, F2025C01030), never copied from the
-- encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.

-- Free access (ss 15-18, 33).
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a fixed phone line (a standard telephone service)` `000` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider must give me access to the emergency call service for 000 and 112, free of charge (ss 15, 16, 33)`
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a mobile phone service` `112` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider must give me access to the emergency call service for 000 and 112, free of charge (ss 15, 16, 33)`
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a mobile phone service` `000` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider must give me access to the emergency call service for 000 and 112, free of charge (ss 15, 16, 33)`
-- 112 from a fixed line: the Determination puts no duty on it.
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a fixed phone line (a standard telephone service)` `112` FALSE EQUALS `no duty for this number on this service: use 000 (or 112 on a mobile)`
-- A Deaf caller using a TTY on a fixed line calls 106.
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a fixed phone line (a standard telephone service)` `106 (the text emergency number)` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider must give me access to the 106 text emergency call service, free of charge (ss 17, 18, 33)`
-- A satellite handset that can also use a mobile network, 112.
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a satellite service, through a handset that can also use a mobile network` `112` FALSE EQUALS `yes: my provider must give me access to the emergency call service for 000 and 112, free of charge (ss 15, 16, 33)`
-- A boat's fixed Inmarsat terminal: exempt.
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `an exempt satellite service (a non-handheld Inmarsat device, not under the universal service obligation)` `000` FALSE EQUALS `no: an exempt satellite service cannot be used for emergency calls, and my provider had to tell me so in writing before first supplying it (ss 12(2)(b), 13)`
-- Mains power failure took out the NBN modem.
#ASSERT `Must my provider give me free access to emergency calls` `a fixed phone line (a standard telephone service)` `000` TRUE EQUALS `not while a law requires or authorises my provider to stop it (for example a police request to suspend the service), or a matter beyond its control (a power failure at my premises, damaged wiring, my own call barring) prevents it (s 12)`
#ASSERT `Can I call emergency services without a number issued to me`

-- Call information (s 23).
#ASSERT `What must go with my emergency call` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my phone number, as far as practicable, and the most precise location information available when I call (s 23(2), (4))`
#ASSERT `What must go with my emergency call` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the most precise location information available when I call; my number need not be sent because my mobile provider cannot identify it (s 23(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `What must go with my emergency call` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my phone number, as far as practicable, and the most precise location information available when I call (s 23(2), (4))`

-- Welfare checks (s 28).
#ASSERT `Must my provider do a welfare check` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my provider do a welfare check` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my provider do a welfare check` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my provider do a welfare check` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my provider do a welfare check` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- Incompatible mobiles (ss 64-71).
#ASSERT `What must my provider do about my incompatible phone` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my provider must tell me, must not supply service to this phone, and must tell me about other phones, including low cost or no cost ones (ss 64, 65)`
#ASSERT `What must my provider do about my incompatible phone` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my provider must tell me within 5 business days that it will cut off service to this phone 28 to 35 days later, send two more notices first, tell me about other phones including low cost or no cost ones, and offer help through its payment assistance policy if I am in financial hardship (ss 68 to 70)`
#ASSERT `What must my provider do about my incompatible phone` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as a short-stay foreign traveller I need only be sent a notice that the phone cannot reach the emergency call service; supply need not stop (s 71)`
#ASSERT `What must my provider do about my incompatible phone` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing: my phone can reach the emergency call service on my provider's network and, if it is down, on other networks`
-- First notice 1 March 2027: cut-off no earlier than 29 March 2027 and no later than 5 April 2027.
#ASSERT `The earliest day my provider may stop service to my phone` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 29 3 2027
#ASSERT `The latest day my provider must stop service to my phone` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 5 4 2027

-- The s 69 duties (times in days). Notice on day 3; supply ceased on day 33, 30 days after the notice. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `the s 69 duties` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `notify me that my phone can no longer reach the emergency call service` AT 3
    (WAITUNTIL 32)
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `cease supply to my phone` AT 33
-- Supply cut on day 13, 10 days after the notice. Expected: BREACH (s 69(4)(a)).
#TRACE `the s 69 duties` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `notify me that my phone can no longer reach the emergency call service` AT 3
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `cease supply to my phone` AT 13
-- Two further notices sent. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `the s 69(3) further notices` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `send me a further notification` AT 10
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `send me a further notification` AT 20
